{"name":"Close Knit","hex":"#d5d6cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"close-knit","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a group: closely connected or linked, as by a common bond, culture, or identity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/close-knit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Close-Knit","blocks":[{"text":"Close-Knit  is a 2017 Japanese drama film directed by Naoko Ogigami. Ogigami wrote the script after a visit to the United States caused her to become more aware of LGBT issues. The film follows Tomo Ogawa, an 11-year-old girl, who becomes close to her uncle's transgender girlfriend after Tomo's mother, who has been raising her alone, unexpectedly runs off and leaves Tomo behind. It was screened in the Panorama section at the 67th Berlin International Film Festival."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Close-Knit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Close-Knit"},{"title":"Knitting","blocks":[{"text":"Knitting is the process of interlooping yarn to create textile fabric made of interconnected loops, done by hand, machine or both."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Oma_strickt_Str%C3%BCmpfe.jpg/330px-Oma_strickt_Str%C3%BCmpfe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knitting"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Eureka_Knitting_Silk_for_hand_knitting%2C_half_ounce._-_DPLA_-_cf08334529ffa81f9c6eb16763cddb9b_%28page_1%29.jpg/500px-Eureka_Knitting_Silk_for_hand_knitting%2C_half_ounce._-_DPLA_-_cf08334529ffa81f9c6eb16763cddb9b_%28page_1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Eureka_Knitting_Silk_for_hand_knitting%2C_half_ounce._-_DPLA_-_cf08334529ffa81f9c6eb16763cddb9b_%28page_1%29.jpg/1280px-Eureka_Knitting_Silk_for_hand_knitting%2C_half_ounce._-_DPLA_-_cf08334529ffa81f9c6eb16763cddb9b_%28page_1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Eureka_Knitting_Silk_for_hand_knitting%2C_half_ounce._-_DPLA_-_cf08334529ffa81f9c6eb16763cddb9b_%28page_1%29.jpg/500px-Eureka_Knitting_Silk_for_hand_knitting%2C_half_ounce._-_DPLA_-_cf08334529ffa81f9c6eb16763cddb9b_%28page_1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eureka Knitting Silk for hand knitting, half ounce, c. 1870–1900; from the 19th Century American Trade Cards collection of the Boston Public Library","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEureka_Knitting_Silk_for_hand_knitting%2C_half_ounce._-_DPLA_-_cf08334529ffa81f9c6eb16763cddb9b_(page_1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Single_crochet_swatch.jpg/500px-Single_crochet_swatch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Single_crochet_swatch.jpg/1280px-Single_crochet_swatch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Single_crochet_swatch.jpg/500px-Single_crochet_swatch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASingle_crochet_swatch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Knit_stockinette_stitch.jpg/500px-Knit_stockinette_stitch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Knit_stockinette_stitch.jpg/1280px-Knit_stockinette_stitch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Knit_stockinette_stitch.jpg/500px-Knit_stockinette_stitch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKnit_stockinette_stitch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Knit-schematic.png/500px-Knit-schematic.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Knit-schematic.png/500px-Knit-schematic.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Structure of stockinette stitch, a common weave in knitted fabric. The meandering red path defines one course, the path of the yarn through the fabric. The uppermost white loops are unsecured and \"active\", but they secure the red loops suspended from them. In turn, the red loops secure the white loops just below them, which in turn secure the loops below them, and so on.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKnit-schematic.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Knitting_wales_slip_stitch.png/500px-Knitting_wales_slip_stitch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Knitting_wales_slip_stitch.png/500px-Knitting_wales_slip_stitch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alternating wales of red and yellow knit stitches. Each stitch in a wale is suspended from the one above it.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKnitting_wales_slip_stitch.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Trikot.jpg/330px-Trikot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Trikot.jpg/330px-Trikot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Basic pattern of warp knitting. Parallel yarns zigzag lengthwise along the fabric, each loop securing a loop of an adjacent strand from the previous row.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATrikot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Rundstrickmaschine_Zungennadeln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Rundstrickmaschine_Zungennadeln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"A modern knitting machine in the process of weft knitting","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARundstrickmaschine_Zungennadeln.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Knitting_knit_and_purl_stitches.png/500px-Knitting_knit_and_purl_stitches.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Knitting_knit_and_purl_stitches.png/500px-Knitting_knit_and_purl_stitches.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In the knit stitch on the left, the next (red) loop passes through the previous (yellow) loop from below, whereas in the purl stitch (right), the next stitch enters from above. Thus, a knit stitch on one side of the fabric appears as a purl stitch on the other, and vice versa.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKnitting_knit_and_purl_stitches.png"}],"sounds":{"close-knit":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/83/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-close-knit.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/83/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-close-knit.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-cl